# Level two

The second browse level lists detailed destinations within a subtopic, either curated or alphabetically ordered. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/mainstream-browse/level-two/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use this level for a focused set of guides, device instructions or settings explanations. At this point people should be able to select a task directly rather than navigate through another vague category. Include short descriptions where two destinations sound similar.

## Structure and behaviour

Give the page a specific subtopic title and a route to its parent. Choose an order intentionally: the user’s likely sequence for a procedure, or alphabetical order for known-item lookup. Make each link’s destination type clear when mixing a guide, native page and external document.

## Home Assistant boundary

The example subtopics are documentation structures, not installed HA routes. Avoid hidden accordion groups that make a short list harder to scan. Do not imply that changing the browse order changes device priority or automation behaviour.

